Ten minutes later, the next customer comes to the counter.
"A cappuccino, please," he says warmly.
I take a deep breath.
This is my second coffee.
I focus on the machine.
I am currently learning to stay calm under pressure.
First, I grind the beans.
Then I start the water.
The espresso does not run too fast this time.
Now I froth the milk.
I paid close attention to Elif's hands.
She showed me earlier how to do it right.
The milk is warm and beautifully creamy.
Fortunately, I didn't spill anything.
I pour the milk carefully into the cup.
"Here is your cappuccino," I say to the man.
He tastes the coffee immediately.
He nods and smiles at me.
"Very tasty, thank you!" he says.
I am incredibly relieved.
Elif looks at me and nods with satisfaction.
